  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The structure of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>-</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;ion is:</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/892a9025-f173-4f49-8179-2293cdf43844-image.png\" style=\"width: 150px; height: 77px;\" /></p><p>As we can see central atom has 3 lone pair and two bond pair and outer atoms has 3 lone pair each. So, there are total of 9 lone pair. Central atom will have&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></math>&nbsp;hybridisation and linear shape.</p></blockquote>",
